    {
      "id": "lk-journey",
      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "FROM GAME JAM TO VERTICAL SLICE",
      "body": "Lightkeeper did not begin as Lightkeeper. It started as Fell Out, a small game-jam project built around a strange archipelago, its inhabitants, and a world hidden behind fog. We liked the setting enough to keep returning to it.\n\nIn 2024, Fell Out received concept funding from FFF Bayern. The job changed from “we made a fun little game” to “can this become an actual product?” We built a high-concept pitch, expanded the world, and tested exploration, gathering, traversal, progression and character interaction at a much larger scale.\n\nLater that year the project, now Lightkeeper, received prototype funding. The prototype phase expanded the game again, but it also forced us to cut. The final vertical slice is the result of that path. This archive keeps the polished work next to discarded directions and technical tests because the interesting part is how the project changed every time we learned something new.",
      "source": "",
      "mediaRef": "",
      "href": "",
      "label": "",
      "projectId": "",
      "alt": "",
      "fit": "cover"
    },
